# The chords alone, written for gohar, in C: II-V everywhere, each a
# tone or a half tone from the last, in C, D, G, G♭, then in F and in G
# for the bridge. An AABA: the first A ends on a turnaround, the second
# on C held, the last A recalls the first.

{start_of_grid label="A" shape="4x4"}
| Dm7 G7 | Dm7 G7 | Em7 A7 | Em7 A7 |
| Am7 D7 | Abm7 Db7 | Cmaj7 F7 | Em7 A7 |.
{end_of_grid}
{start_of_grid label="A2" shape="4x4"}
| Dm7 G7 | Dm7 G7 | Em7 A7 | Em7 A7 |
| Am7 D7 | Abm7 Db7 | Cmaj7 | % |.
{end_of_grid}
{start_of_grid label="B" shape="4x4"}
| Gm7 C7 | Gm7 C7 | Fmaj7 | % |
| Am7 D7 | Am7 D7 | G7 | % |.
{end_of_grid}
{x_play: A}
